member.example:
Example usage:
```csharp
public class MyStateObserver : IAsyncStateObserver
{
  public async ValueTask OnStateEntered(NodeId id, CancellationToken ct = default)
  {
     Console.WriteLine($"State {id} entered.");
  }

  public async ValueTask OnStateExited(NodeId id, CancellationToken ct = default)
  {
     Console.WriteLine($"State {id} exited.");
  }

  public async ValueTask OnTransition(NodeId from, NodeId to, CancellationToken ct = default)
  {
     Console.WriteLine($"Transition from {from} to {to}.");
  }
}
var observer = new MyStateObserver();
var stateMachine = new AsyncStateMachine(graph, observer);
await stateMachine.ExecuteAsync();
```

member.summary:
Shared plumbing for the owned-board walk: the linear probe over one graph's nodes (the
 shape — async-then-sync logic slots, no recursion of its own;
composites recurse by walking their child machines) and the path composition helpers.

Controls what a state machine should do after it reaches a terminal status
(, , or
).

Executes the current node. Returns  when the machine
transitions to a next node, or a terminal result ( /
) when the run is finished.

Resolution through decorator layers, shared by the wiring walks and the machines'
construction-time report tables. Cold path by contract (construction / run-start walks);
the per-layer step is two type tests, no allocation.

Per-node "this join has fired at least once this run" flags (indexed by node index;
empty when the graph has no joins). Distinguishes benign quorum leftovers from join
starvation after a resume.
